  "Humorist and novelist; the creator of Jeeves and Bertie Wooster, and the finest comic prose writer in English.",
  "Born Pelham Grenville Wodehouse at Guildford on 15 October 1881; he worked in a bank and then as a comic writer for the London magazines, creating Psmith in 1903 and publishing My Man Jeeves in 1919. Right Ho, Jeeves (1934), The Code of the Woosters (1938), Blandings Castle (1935) and some ninety books followed. He lived in America from 1914 and died at Southampton, New York, on 14 February 1975.",
