  "Born in Perth on 26 August 1875, the son of a Free Church minister; he was educated at Glasgow and Oxford, worked in South Africa with Milner, and served as a war correspondent and in intelligence. The Thirty-Nine Steps (1915), Greenmantle (1916), The Three Hostages (1924), Sick Heart River (1941) and the histories followed, and he was Governor-General of Canada from 1935. He died in Montreal on 11 February 1940.",
