  "Born Henry Maximilian Beerbohm in Kensington on 24 August 1872; he went from Charterhouse to Oxford, published The Works of Max Beerbohm in 1896 and became the drama critic of the Saturday Review in 1898. Zuleika Dobson (1911), Seven Men (1919) and A Christmas Garland (1912), the greatest book of parodies in English, followed. He lived in Rapallo from 1910 and died there on 20 May 1956.",
